  "term": "paramnesia",
  "definition": "Paramnesia is a memory defect in which recollection is distorted or illusory, producing a false memory rather than a simple failure to remember. It includes mistaken recall such as false familiarity, wrong placement in time or order, or imagined additions to real events.",
